WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.969
 

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:17.050
In six hours, you, your government,

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:21.688
and 124 million other people across 14 states

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:26.659
will be tested by the greatest disaster
to ever hit the U.S. East Coast.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:30.130
A great wave,
1000 meters (3280 ft.) tall,

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.233
moving towards you at
1000 km/h (621 mph),

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.635
and that's only the beginning.

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.879
This is 'What If,'

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:49.749
and here's what would happen if a
megatsunami hit the U.S. East Coast.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:55.021
Unlike most tsunamis that are
triggered by tectonic activity,

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:58.992
megatsunamis are caused
by sudden impact.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:02.962
A huge chunk of debris, possibly a meteor,
smashes the water,

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:07.467
creating a huge wave, which might
reach thousands of meters high.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:12.839
The initial super wave would set off a chain
reaction of smaller waves in all directions.

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:19.546
But by smaller, we really mean they'd be about
100 meters (328 ft.) high instead of 1000.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:22.248
Depending on the size and
location of the impact,

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.551
and the speed of the
waves racing towards you,

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:26.953
you may get a few hours warning.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.923
But will that be enough time?

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:33.793
Welcome to La Palma,
one of the 7 main Canary Islands,

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:38.798
home to 81,000 people,
and a giant, scary volcano.

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.634
Suppose it erupts, and
the eruption is big enough

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.170
that it triggers a massive landslide.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:48.808
Massive enough, to send over a billion tons
of rock sliding into the ocean, causing...

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:51.177
a megatsunami.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:54.848
The initial wave is
914 meters (3000 feet) high.

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:57.517
It surges upwards and outwards,

00:01:57.517 --> 00:02:01.354
setting off a chain reaction of
deadly waves in all directions.

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:06.726
In 6 hours, a series of 30 meter (100 ft) waves
will batter the American East Coast.

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:07.660
Ramming speed:

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.795
"Ramming speed."

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.463
"Ramming speed!"

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.534
900 km/h (560 mph).

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:17.537
One of the 7 Deep-ocean
Assessment and Reporting buoys

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.939
floating along the Atlantic Coast
will undoubtedly

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.275
register this mega-displacement of water,

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:27.313
giving the U.S. Tsunami Warning Center time
to alert anyone who might be in danger.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:31.985
The only problem is, that's 38%
of the American population.

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:34.821
The entire U.S. East Coast
would be affected,

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:38.725
putting 14 states, and 124 million people,

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:41.895
including key members of
the government, at risk.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.731
If you can't make it out in time, then climb.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:47.667
In major cities, the newest
and tallest skyscrapers

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.969
would be the safest places to go.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:53.473
And your own safety will
be entirely your responsibility,

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:55.975
since emergency services
wouldn't really be able

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:59.012
to take action until the onslaught was over.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:03.016
In the best case scenario, you've managed
to evade the disaster completely.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:06.953
Your family is safe, but your home,
not so much.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:11.124
Worse, you're on the roof of a skyscraper,
safe, with a group of survivors,

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:15.995
waiting for a helicopter to come pick you up,
which might take a very long time.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:19.599
But in the worst case scenario...

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.701
The death toll would be staggering;

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:26.506
the economic impact, easily costing
billions, if not trillions of dollars.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:29.275
It will take decades to rebuild, and yet,

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:32.712
is it wrong to suggest that we
might've gotten off easy?

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:37.183
How much worse would it have been
without the 6 hours of advance notice?

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:42.155
That's right, you owe a big thank you to these
super smart buoys monitoring the coast,

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:45.158
keeping you safe and dry,
so that you can rest easy,

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:48.861
and keep watching 'What If.'

